1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,614
Some values belong to the whole site:

2
00:00:03,614 --> 00:00:06,715
an announcement, a contact address, a switch.

3
00:00:06,715 --> 00:00:11,518
Custom Settings turns a content type into a section of the Settings menu.

4
00:00:11,518 --> 00:00:15,956
You create one, edit its values, control who can change it, and add

5
00:00:15,956 --> 00:00:17,780
it to a deployment plan.

6
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:26,830
Site settings are values that belong to the whole site, not to one page.

7
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:31,451
The Settings menu groups them into sections, such as General and Debugging.

8
00:00:31,451 --> 00:00:34,190
Custom Settings adds sections of your own.

9
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:38,675
A content type describes the fields of one kind of content.

10
00:00:38,675 --> 00:00:43,444
Give it the CustomSettings stereotype, a label that marks its purpose, and it

11
00:00:43,444 --> 00:00:46,030
becomes a section of the Settings menu.

12
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:49,065
Its fields become the form you fill in.

13
00:00:49,065 --> 00:00:52,721
The values are saved with the site settings, so they do not appear

14
00:00:52,721 --> 00:00:54,498
in the list of content items.

15
00:00:54,498 --> 00:00:57,240
A site holds one set of values for each section.

16
00:00:57,990 --> 00:01:01,296
Create a separate content type for every section.

17
00:01:01,296 --> 00:01:05,745
Do not give the stereotype to a type that already has content items:

18
00:01:05,745 --> 00:01:08,210
the documentation warns against it.

19
00:01:12,399 --> 00:01:15,012
Custom Settings is a feature of its own.

20
00:01:15,012 --> 00:01:19,045
If it is not enabled on your site, open Tools, then Features, and

21
00:01:19,045 --> 00:01:20,919
search for Custom Settings.

22
00:01:21,372 --> 00:01:23,859
Select Enable next to Custom Settings.

23
00:01:23,859 --> 00:01:26,912
A message confirms that the feature was enabled.

24
00:01:31,102 --> 00:01:33,676
A section starts as a content type.

25
00:01:33,676 --> 00:01:38,762
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and select Create new type.

26
00:01:39,226 --> 00:01:42,014
Enter Announcement Banner as the Display Name.

27
00:01:42,014 --> 00:01:46,893
The Technical Name fills in from it, and the saved values are stored under that name.

28
00:01:46,893 --> 00:01:47,966
Select Create.

29
00:01:48,418 --> 00:01:52,177
A message confirms the type, and the Add Parts page opens.

30
00:01:52,177 --> 00:01:55,642
A type can have parts, which add ready-made behavior.

31
00:01:55,642 --> 00:01:58,638
This one needs only fields, so select Cancel.

32
00:01:59,091 --> 00:02:01,718
The Fields section of the type is empty.

33
00:02:01,718 --> 00:02:03,031
Select Add Field.

34
00:02:03,497 --> 00:02:06,258
Enter Banner Text as the Display Name.

35
00:02:06,258 --> 00:02:10,651
The Field Type list offers Boolean Field, Text Field and others.

36
00:02:10,651 --> 00:02:13,287
Choose Text Field, then select Save.

37
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:16,068
Add a second field the same way.

38
00:02:16,068 --> 00:02:21,298
Name it Show Banner, choose Boolean Field, which is a checkbox, and select Save.

39
00:02:21,753 --> 00:02:27,378
A type starts with Creatable, Listable, Draftable, Versionable and Securable checked.

40
00:02:27,378 --> 00:02:31,953
A settings section needs none of them, so clear all five checkboxes.

41
00:02:32,421 --> 00:02:33,446
Select Save.

42
00:02:33,446 --> 00:02:37,833
Do this before you set the stereotype, because the editor hides most of

43
00:02:37,833 --> 00:02:40,511
these options once a stereotype is saved.

44
00:02:40,963 --> 00:02:44,336
Back in the list, select Edit for Announcement Banner.

45
00:02:44,336 --> 00:02:47,373
Then enter CustomSettings in the Stereotype box.

46
00:02:47,829 --> 00:02:48,889
Select Save.

47
00:02:48,889 --> 00:02:53,129
A message confirms the update, and the type is a settings section.

48
00:02:57,318 --> 00:02:58,953
Open Settings in the menu.

49
00:02:58,953 --> 00:03:03,704
Announcement Banner is listed beside the sections that Orchard Core provides, under the

50
00:03:03,704 --> 00:03:05,288
display name of the type.

51
00:03:05,752 --> 00:03:08,540
The page shows the two fields of the type.

52
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:12,782
Enter a message in Banner Text, check Show Banner, and select Save.

53
00:03:13,238 --> 00:03:18,665
A message confirms that the site settings were updated, and the page shows the saved values.

54
00:03:18,665 --> 00:03:22,098
Templates and code can read them from the site settings.

55
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:29,033
Every section has a permission of its own.

56
00:03:29,033 --> 00:03:34,100
No role receives it automatically, but the Administrator role has every permission.

57
00:03:34,554 --> 00:03:40,334
To grant it, open Access Control, then Roles, and select Edit for the Editor role.

58
00:03:40,788 --> 00:03:43,552
Search the permissions for Announcement Banner.

59
00:03:43,552 --> 00:03:48,248
Manage Custom Settings - Announcement Banner is listed in the Custom Settings group.

60
00:03:48,702 --> 00:03:50,578
Check Allow and select Save.

61
00:03:50,578 --> 00:03:54,386
Members of the Editor role can open the section under Settings.

62
00:03:54,386 --> 00:03:57,752
Roles without the permission do not see it in the menu.

63
00:04:01,943 --> 00:04:05,713
A deployment plan can carry the values to another site.

64
00:04:05,713 --> 00:04:10,843
Open Tools, Deployments, Plans, and select Manage Steps for an existing plan.

65
00:04:11,304 --> 00:04:12,717
Select Add Step.

66
00:04:12,717 --> 00:04:17,084
In Available Steps, filter for Custom Settings and select Add.

67
00:04:17,538 --> 00:04:22,111
Include all custom settings is checked, which exports every section.

68
00:04:22,111 --> 00:04:25,015
Clear it to pick the sections to include.

69
00:04:25,015 --> 00:04:27,548
Leave it checked and select Create.

70
00:04:27,999 --> 00:04:28,254
The plan lists the Custom Settings step with the badge All.

71
00:04:28,254 --> 00:04:28,408
The step carries the values only.

72
00:04:28,408 --> 00:04:28,719
To move the content type as well, add an Update Content Definitions step.

73
00:04:30,719 --> 00:04:35,163
A content type with the CustomSettings stereotype becomes a section of the Settings

74
00:04:35,163 --> 00:04:36,960
menu, with its own permission.

75
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,259
Thanks for watching.

